      "text": "To find the value of \\( x \\) given that \\( x^2 = 729 \\), we need to isolate \\( x \\). We start with the equation:\n\n\\[\nx^2 = 729\n\\]\n\nNext, we take the square root of both sides to solve for \\( x \\). Remember that when you take the square root, you must consider both the positive and negative roots:\n\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt{729} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = -\\sqrt{729}\n\\]\n\nWe calculate \\( \\sqrt{729} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{729} = 27\n\\]\n\nThus, we have two possible values for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = 27 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = -27\n\\]\n\nSince the problem states that \\( x \\) is positive, we discard the negative solution. Therefore, the value of \\( x \\) is:\n\n\\[\nx = 27\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27}\n\\]",
